+# #139 Classify the pytest inventory Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers** Use Superpowers subagent-driven development or executing-plans after separate implementation authorization. Checkboxes describe the authorized attempt.
+
+**Goal** Classify complete pytest collections into deterministic, scoped obligations and reconcile the full result against the delivered #138 comparison.
+
+**Architecture** An offline classifier validates explicit collection profiles and projects rows using reviewed test rules and supplied #103 policy. A private comparison harness exercises the same classifier against retained exact inputs with evidence kind preserved.
+
+**Tech stack** Python 3.13.9, uv 0.10.6, locked pytest and Ruff, standard-library JSON and SHA-256.
+
+**Spec** [Own #139 design](../design/2026-11-10-139-classify-pytest-inventory-design.md) · [Accepted #133 T02](https://github.com/kburson/aitm/blob/dbe0d68b3e7b977c9fbf51e26d9ae8c6f629af84/.aitm/stories/001/133/plan/test-impact-analysis-implementation-plan.md#L187) · [JIT inputs](2026-11-10-139-jit.md)
+
+## Global constraints
+
+- Keep #103 authoritative. Work in an isolated branch after separate implementation authority. Preserve existing Python job targets, unrounded product and helper floors, optional skips, required child evidence, installed-wheel smoke, and exact PR-base comparison.
+- Own `tools/ci/tia/inventory.py`, `tools/ci/tia/suites.json` and `tools/ci/tests/test_tia_inventory.py` only. Keep the implicit `tia` namespace and use the existing package toolchain. No workflow, observer, verifier, baseline, snapshot, package, protection or #158 changes.
+- Retain private raw evidence in custody. Publish only sanitized provenance, counts and digests. The inventory is an offline projection, and its hosted source label only describes the verified input supplied by the trusted caller.
+
+## Review focus
+
+- A parameter may contain a slash, brackets, or platform name. The exact ID survives and capability still comes from the observed runner scope.
+- A previously unseen file, missing required profile, duplicate node, wrong capability, incompatible role or incomplete collection holds the result.
+- The console smoke node lives under CI tooling but runs with product and emits `cli-help`. Helper IDs remain separately owned, with hosted per-node results unavailable in the comparison.
+- A valid optional capability skip retains its ID and exact reason. A deselection, unexpected skip, xfail, or omitted mandatory node cannot masquerade as complete collection.
+- Local, synthetic and qualified hosted provenance cannot collapse to one identity even for equal rows. Historical #103 evidence remains comparison input.
+
+## Task 1 · Implement the classifier and approved policy
+
+**Interface.** Export `classify(collection: bytes, suite_policy: SuitePolicy) -> Inventory`. `SuitePolicy` is a frozen two-field record with `suites: bytes` and `ci103: bytes`. `Inventory` is the canonical UTF-8 JSON bytes for `aitm.tia-inventory/v1`. Raise `ValueError` with a stable category for malformed input, scope or capability, collection, or policy mismatch.
+
+| Record | Required fields |
+| --- | --- |
+| Normalized collection `aitm.tia-collection/v1` | `schema`, `kind` (`local_advisory` or `hosted_collection_proof`), `repository`, `snapshot`, `profile`, `required_scopes`, `scopes`. Local snapshot carries `content_digest`. Hosted snapshot carries `commit`, `tree`, `ref`, `run_id` and `run_attempt`. The trusted caller supplies the intended profile and required scope domain. |
+| Scope row | `id`, `runner`, `capabilities`, `observer`, `controls`, `receipt_sha256`, `exit_code`, `complete`, `deselected`, `items`, optional `source_reference`. The reference is an original evidence kind, exact tree and receipt digest, with run and attempt when present. Items carry `nodeid`, `disposition` (`collected` or `allowed_skip`) and `reason` only for the latter. Qualifying `hosted_collection_proof` is a T07/T08 responsibility. |
+| Suite rules `aitm.tia-suite-policy/v1` | `schema`, `profiles`, `runners`, `modules`, `overrides`. Profiles `product-base`, `product-cli` and `ci-helpers` constrain applicable owner/targets, required capabilities and #103 obligations. Runner profiles name supported scope and required capabilities. Module rows carry owner, suite and isolation. Overrides are exact module/function selectors with suite, isolation, extra capabilities, mandatory CLI flag or child labels as applicable. |
+| Inventory `aitm.tia-inventory/v1` | `schema`, `kind`, `repository`, `snapshot`, `profile`, `suite_policy_sha256`, `ci103_policy_sha256`, ordered `scopes`, ordered `obligations`. Scope identities retain runner, capabilities, observer, controls, receipt and any source reference. Each row contains `provider`, `owner`, `platform_scope`, `nodeid`, `suite`, `isolation_group`, `required_capabilities`, `mandatory`, `optional_skip_reason`, `required_children`, `disposition`. Its digest is SHA-256 of the full output bytes. |
+
+- [ ] Add a valid small fixture in `test_tia_inventory.py` and the two accepted cases below. Import the public function as `from tia.inventory import classify`. Run the cases and retain red evidence at that public call before implementing the projection.
+
+  | Test | Assertion |
+  | --- | --- |
+  | `test_classification_preserves_parametrized_platform_ids` | The same complete opaque parameterized ID under two explicit allowed scopes yields two sorted keys. A second parameter value stays distinct. Native APFS/ACL and process group labels come from reviewed rules. Changing receipt/provenance while retaining IDs changes the canonical digest. Reordering the input scope/item lists leaves the projected output stable when receipt identities are unchanged. |
+  | `test_unclassified_or_duplicate_fails` | Parameterize one mutation at a time for an unknown module, duplicate node, repeated/missing/extra scope, missing required capability or node, malformed source path, overlap in policy, duplicate JSON key, nonzero exit, incomplete collection, deselection and unexpected skip/xfail. Each fails closed with a reason category. |
+  | `test_ci103_scope_and_child_mapping` | Assert all six mandatory product IDs, the optional firmlink allowance and reason, exactly two required child labels in product-plus-CLI, product ownership of the installed CLI and helper ownership of all four helper targets. Base scope expects product only. An exact allowed skip retains its obligation. |
+
+- [ ] Implement the strict parser and projection. Validate source path segments before matching exact module paths and the unparameterized function-qualified selector. Split the source at the first `::`, then find the parameter suffix in the opaque remainder for matching only. Refuse duplicate keys, unsupported schemas and non-finite JSON. Hash the actual supplied policy bytes. Serialize sorted object keys, compact separators, UTF-8, no ASCII escape conversion or trailing newline. Sort obligations by their complete tuple, scope rows by scope ID, and unordered metadata sets consistently. Keep the transformation free of filesystem reads and network calls.
+- [ ] Encode the exact rules in the design in `suites.json`. Read the #103 required product IDs and optional allowance from the supplied existing policy. Cross-check the required child labels and their mapped tests, profile applicability, and capability declarations. Run the same focused tests to green.
+
+## Task 2 · Reconcile evidence and verify delivery
+
+- [ ] Validate the canonical #138 bytes against the JIT digest. Replay the 592 historical base IDs, both separate 630 product-plus-CLI roles and the 182 advisory helper IDs against their profile using exact IDs, roles and capabilities. Use the historical archived policy when applicable. For offline projection tests, use a local fixture observation carrying the explicit `source_reference` kind `ci103_historical_replay`, preserving verified historical evidence and its limits separately. Never pass a #103 replay as a qualified hosted TIA collection. Compare exact row key sets back to each input, confirm equal PR/push IDs with distinct provenance, and check outcomes, mandatory cases, skip allowances and child labels against the original receipts. No hosted helper per-node outcomes are established.
+- [ ] Reconcile the exact current 748 product-plus-CLI IDs from the pinned push, retaining the baseline-to-current difference listed in the JIT. Verify the four helper test source blobs and collection controls against the historical ones, then run the current four-target collect-only check and compare exact helper node sets. Treat any drift as a scoped discrepancy requiring a verified explanation. Save private raw outputs and a sanitized reconciliation of profile, counts, hashes, ownership, suite totals and capability groups.
+- [ ] Run V(inventory), neighboring tests and Ruff from the physical source root. Run the current full local suite and documented required CI for exact delivery.
+
+  ```sh
+  PYTHONPATH="$PWD/tools/ci" uv run --project packages/aitm-usage --locked \
+    pytest -q tools/ci/tests/test_tia_inventory.py
+  PYTHONPATH="$PWD/tools/ci" uv run --project packages/aitm-usage --locked \
+    pytest -q tools/ci/tests/test_tia_baseline.py tools/ci/tests/test_tia_snapshot.py
+  uv run --project packages/aitm-usage --locked ruff check \
+    --config packages/aitm-usage/pyproject.toml tools/ci
+  uv run --project packages/aitm-usage --locked ruff format --check \
+    --config packages/aitm-usage/pyproject.toml tools/ci
+  ```
+
+- [ ] Commit the three owned files only. Retain exact-head local Test, independent source review and same-attempt #103 hosted proof. The verifier treats additions under `tools/ci/` as changed controls. Obtain the applicable exact tested-tree disposition through the existing authority before the trusted-target verifier, then follow the normal delivery and Close requirements when authorized.
+
+Estimate **3.5 implementation agent-hours**. Classifier, policy and focused red/green 2h. Exact reconciliation and local checks 1h. Evidence packaging and handoff 0.5h. Review, approvals and hosted queue are separate. Return to refinement if work would exceed four implementation agent-hours or if the baseline comparison cannot be reconstructed from verified evidence.
